{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill","id":968187,"title":"The Crafting Skill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-12T15:31:41-07:00","id":968187,"title":"The Crafting Skill","content":"So, &quot;crafting&quot; strikes me as a pretty odd duck. It seems odd to me that one skill covers everything from auto repairs to forgery to sculpting.<br /> <br /> For you experienced STs out there, how do you handle this? Do you assume that anyone with crafting can just... kind of do anything with their hands? Or do you force players to buy crafting skills independently of one another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:40:20-07:00","id":968194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill#post968187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, &quot;crafting&quot; strikes me as a pretty odd duck. It seems odd to me that one skill covers everything from auto repairs to forgery to sculpting.<br /> <br /> For you experienced STs out there, how do you handle this? Do you assume that anyone with crafting can just... kind of do anything with their hands? Or do you force players to buy crafting skills independently of one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>We use it for everything from cooking to arts and crafts to explosives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:49:24-07:00","id":968203,"title":"","content":"I largely treat it as an engineering/mechanics/demolitions skill, though architecture definitely fits in there too. Anything beyond that is a Specialty or another skill; sculpture is definitely Expression to me, for one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T15:59:54-07:00","id":968214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill#post968187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, &quot;crafting&quot; strikes me as a pretty odd duck. It seems odd to me that one skill covers everything from auto repairs to forgery to sculpting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that makes it an oddity among CofD Skills. Athletics covers everything from swimming to pole vaulting to archery. Science covers everything from evolutionary biology to geology to theoretical physics. Drive covers everything from cars to submarines to horse-drawn carriages. Most of the Skills are extremely broad, and meant to be differentiated via Specializations, if anything is odd it's the Brawl/Weaponry division for being unusually specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill#post968187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For you experienced STs out there, how do you handle this? Do you assume that anyone with crafting can just... kind of do anything with their hands? Or do you force players to buy crafting skills independently of one another?</div> </div> </div> </div>Specializations are the tool for... Well... Specializing. If a player wants to make a character who's an expert auto mechanic but not a great stonemason, they can take 1-2 dots in Crafts, a Specialty in motor vehicles, and the Area of Expertise and Automotove Genius Merits. If they just want a generalized &quot;I can fix anything&quot; character, they can take 4-5 dots in Crafts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:03:42-07:00","id":968218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill?p=968214#post968214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that makes it an oddity among CofD Skills. Athletics covers everything from swimming to pole vaulting to archery. Science covers everything from evolutionary biology to geology to theoretical physics. Drive covers everything from cars to submarines to horse-drawn carriages. Most of the Skills are extremely broad, and meant to be differentiated via Specializations, if anything is odd it's the Brawl/Weaponry division for being unusually specific.<br /> <br /> <br /> Specializations are the tool for... Well... Specializing. If a player wants to make a character who's an expert auto mechanic but not a great stonemason, they can take 1-2 dots in Crafts, a Specialty in motor vehicles, and the Area of Expertise and Automotove Genius Merits. If they just want a generalized &quot;I can fix anything&quot; character, they can take 4-5 dots in Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right. As I'm digging through the systems, it's becoming more clear how broad the skills are. With judicious use of equipment bonuses and penalties, it actually seems like a very practical way of doing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T16:32:44-07:00","id":968235,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind the what the ranks mean: 3 is above average professional training, 4 is superb, and 5 is a master at their field. It might only seem like a few more XP for one more dice, but as stated, most people &quot;focused&quot; in something pick up Specialties and supporting Merits to represent their skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:25:55-07:00","id":970329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill?p=968214#post968214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that makes it an oddity among CofD Skills. Athletics covers everything from swimming to pole vaulting to archery. Science covers everything from evolutionary biology to geology to theoretical physics. Drive covers everything from cars to submarines to horse-drawn carriages. Most of the Skills are extremely broad, and meant to be differentiated via Specializations, if anything is odd it's the Brawl/Weaponry division for being unusually specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sheer number of melee weaponry, fighting stances, philosophies and precepts around the world is as staggering, trust me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill?p=968214#post968214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specializations are the tool for... Well... Specializing. If a player wants to make a character who's an expert auto mechanic but not a great stonemason, they can take 1-2 dots in Crafts, a Specialty in motor vehicles, and the Area of Expertise and Automotove Genius Merits. If they just want a generalized &quot;I can fix anything&quot; character, they can take 4-5 dots in Crafts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill?p=968218#post968218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. As I'm digging through the systems, it's becoming more clear how broad the skills are. With judicious use of equipment bonuses and penalties, it actually seems like a very practical way of doing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rule of thumb of mine: if the action is sufficiently obscure, say, brain-surgery in medicine, I'd apply a -3 for lacking the necessary specialty (nevermind attaining such a think takes years of education); with an untrained penalty on the skill in question? Not even the most gifted human being can possibly succeed in such an endeavor (IE another -3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:39:42-07:00","id":970339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/968187-the-crafting-skill?p=970329#post970329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rule of thumb of mine: if the action is sufficiently obscure, say, brain-surgery in medicine, I'd apply a -3 for lacking the necessary specialty (nevermind attaining such a think takes years of education); with an untrained penalty on the skill in question? Not even the most gifted human being can possibly succeed in such an endeavor (IE another -3).</div> </div> </div> </div>My group just uses the Medicine skill for, basically, first aid, except for with regards to characters who are specifically doctors. Like I had one once who was literally an oncologist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:16:08-07:00","id":970545,"title":"","content":"In first edition some skill use, such as EOD, required the requisite merit even to attempt no matter how high the skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}